  "body": "## Summary\n- capture normalized web-search tool input and provider output, including answer, result snippets/content, publication metadata, result count, key index, and cost\n- persist a redacted provider/configuration and routing snapshot for every attempt, with configurable capture and size limits\n- add detail/export APIs and an accessible analytics modal for input, response summaries, full results, configuration, and normalized JSON\n- preserve privacy controls with secret-key redaction, URL credential stripping, SHA-256 metadata, bounded truncation envelopes, and 500-character exception capture\n- bump the backward-compatible feature release to 4.13.0 and pin both installers to the deterministic release wheel\n\n## Verification\n- `./scripts/ci.ps1`: 3,002 passed, 38 skipped; suppression, Ruff format/check, ty, and pytest all passed\n- focused websearch/outbound tests: 153 passed in serial mode\n- Windows installer hash scenarios: 12 passed, 6 platform-skipped\n- deterministic wheel rebuilt twice with identical SHA-256\n- local wheel smoke: `free-claude-code 4.13.0`\n- `node --check`, `git diff --check`, and AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md identity check passed\n\n## Release artifact\n- `free_claude_code-4.13.0-py3-none-any.whl`\n- SHA-256: `679565810225215ae3c045cc5c8ef43e4fa53676179ddb1583a25412e811b770`\n\nThe exact prebuilt wheel must be uploaded to the `v4.13.0` GitHub release when this PR is merged; the version-pinned public installer URLs intentionally remain unavailable until that release exists.",
